@{ ViewData["Title"] = "About LinkShield"; }
<section class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">WHY LINKSHIELD</span><h1>Make online safety<br/><em>feel less complicated.</em></h1><p>LinkShield is a student mini-project that demonstrates how a clear interface and explainable rules can support better link awareness.</p></section><section class="about-split"><div class="about-illustration"><div class="big-shield">✓</div><span class="about-note note-a">Privacy-aware demo</span><span class="about-note note-b">Explainable rules</span></div><div class="about-copy"><span class="eyebrow">OUR PURPOSE</span><h2>Awareness before <em>action.</em></h2><p>Suspicious links can arrive through email, messaging apps, social media and even trusted-looking websites. LinkShield checks for a small set of warning patterns and explains what each pattern might mean.</p><p>It is designed for education, not as a replacement for a browser security feature, antivirus software, or a professional threat-intelligence service.</p><div class="feature-list"><div><span>01</span><b>Explainable risk signals</b></div><div><span>02</span><b>History stored in MySQL</b></div><div><span>03</span><b>Practical threat education</b></div></div></div></section><section class="tech-section"><div class="section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">BUILT WITH</span><h2>Modern web fundamentals.</h2></div><div class="tech-grid"><div><b>C# + ASP.NET Core MVC</b><p>Routing, controllers, views and server-side form handling.</p></div><div><b>Entity Framework Core</b><p>Model mapping and database operations through an ORM.</p></div><div><b>MySQL + Pomelo</b><p>Persistent storage for scan records and contact messages.</p></div><div><b>HTML, CSS & JavaScript</b><p>Responsive layout and lightweight client-side interaction.</p></div></div></section>
